; Self test of the port-only fixed form of the TED bug-orig tests
; (tests/bug-orig/CMakeLists.txt): "; @fixed #N Cc", the bug is fixed in
; blitz2-c only.  The expectation holds of TED-C (blitz2 without a file,
; QUIT, the command's output ends with rc=0), so the Cc run must be FIXED
; (exit status 0); the recorded original says the bug shows (written by
; hand), so the C5 run, which does not show it either, is FIXED (0): a real
; test wants REPRODUCED there and fails.
; 99999 is no issue.
; @fixed #99999 Cc
; @source none
; @expect stdout "rc=0"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
